start.heading = Review your Council Tax band
start.title = Review your Council Tax band

start.welsh = This page is also available in
start.welsh.link = Welsh (Cymraeg).

start.whatThisServiceIsFor = What this service is for

start.guidance = This service is provided by the Valuation Office (VO)

start.youCanUseThisServiceTo = You can use this service to:

start.bullet.1 = find out the Council Tax band of any home in England and Wales
start.bullet.2 = check and update the information we have about your home
start.bullet.3 = let us know if you think your Council Tax band is wrong

start.role.heading = The role of the VO

start.role.paragraph = The Valuation Office (VO) puts every home in England and Wales into a group called a 'band'. These bands range from A to I, where band A is the lowest. The VO does not set the amount of Council Tax you pay, send out bills, or collect payments.

start.button = Start now

start.vo.intro = The VO:

start.vo.bullet.1 = values every home in England and Wales and puts them into one of the nine Council Tax bands (Bands A to I)
start.vo.bullet.2 = keeps the list of homes on the Council Tax list up to date
start.vo.bullet.3 = handles challenges from people who think their band is wrong

start.vo.responsible = The VO is responsible for valuing your home and looks at what homes were selling for on that date, not what it is worth today. The band your home is in is based on how much it was worth on 1 April 2003. Find out more about

start.vo.link = Council Tax band ranges.
start.vo.link.url = #

start.council.heading = The role of your local council

start.council.intro = Council Tax is a tax on every home in England and Wales. The money raised by this tax helps pay for things like schools, rubbish collection, emergency services and social care.

start.council.list.intro = Your local council:

start.council.bullet.1 = works out the amount of Council Tax to charge for each band every year
start.council.bullet.2 = sends you your Council Tax bill and collects payments
start.council.bullet.3 = decides how your council tax is spent, for example paying for schools, rubbish collections and emergency services

start.council.outro = Your local council decides how much Council Tax you pay, based on the band your home is in. Your local council is also responsible for any Council Tax discounts, exemptions or reductions you can apply for, such as the Single Person Discount.

start.council.link = Council Tax
start.council.link.url = #

start.before.heading = Before you start

start.before.bullet.1 = to check the Council tax band of a property in England and Wales, you will need a valid postcode and address details for the property
start.before.bullet.2.pre = to view and manage the details of your property, you will need a Government
start.before.bullet.2.link = One Login account
start.before.bullet.2.url = #

start.before.bullet.3.pre = to request a review of your Council Tax band, you may be asked to provide evidence and additional information. You should have this prepared before you start. Find out more about the process of
start.before.bullet.3.link = requesting a band review
start.before.bullet.3.url = #

start.accessibility.pre = If you are unable to use this online service, find out more about
start.accessibility.link = other ways you can access this service
start.accessibility.url = #

